From 1feb03b00c07ce83e167aea279894fd9aa12e3dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Keri <okerixx@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:46:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/47] soundwire: qcom: disable the interrupt before gating
 the clock

swrm_runtime_suspend() can gate hclk while the ClockStopNow interrupt thread still clears status and handles CLK_STOP_FINISHED. On X1E80100 this can corrupt the next clock-stop exit and leave speaker peripherals detached. Disable the main controller IRQ before hclk is gated and re-enable it immediately after hclk returns.

Backport of upstream v2 posting Message-ID: <20261009082639.22662-1-okerixx@gmail.com>

Fixes: 74e79da9fd46 ("soundwire: qcom: add runtime pm support")

Signed-off-by: Oleg Keri <okerixx@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: SP11 Linux Project <272055834+geocausa@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 4e528b8e2..611e61999 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1838,6 +1838,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	clk_prepare_enable(ctrl->hclk);
+	enable_irq(ctrl->irq);
 
 	if (ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported) {
 		reinit_completion(&ctrl->enumeration);
@@ -1921,6 +1922,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	disable_irq(ctrl->irq);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
 
 	usleep_range(300, 305);
